    "proficienciesLanguages": "Armor (Scholar): None\nWeapons (Scholar): Daggers, quarterstaffs (weighted walking canes), darts, slings, Herringer pistols, the Dullards Plinker\nYou can speak, read, and write Common and Cantonese.",
    "features": "Maker’s Mark: Craft-folk and claim engineers offer bench space, parts leads, and introductions. Fancy spark-device work draws investors — and the wrong kind of interest. Unpaid “partners” may appear. Guild-lingo: shop talk of gunsmiths, engineers and tinkers. Not a language, no slot. Without it others miss technical details; when the DM calls it, checks relying on that detail are at disadvantage or fail.",
